IMPORT prelude

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore) -- the employee's questions about one employment: whether the Act covers me
-- (s 2(1)); notice, leaving and being treated as in breach (ss 8, 10, 11, 13, 15); dismissal, suspension and the
-- wrongful-dismissal claim (s 14); when I must be paid (ss 21-24) and what may be taken from my pay (ss 26, 27, 29,
-- 32); whether the rest day, hours and overtime rules cover me and what they pay (ss 35, 37, 38(4), Fourth Schedule);
-- retrenchment benefit (s 45); maternity pay and protection (ss 76, 80(3), 81, 83); annual and sick leave (ss 88A,
-- 89); my key employment terms (s 95A); and whether and by when my retrenchment must be reported (s 96A with the
-- Employment (Retrenchment Reporting) Notification 2019).
--
-- SEAT: the employee -- one person, in one employment with one employer. Every decision is phrased as that person
-- would ask it, from facts that person could state. Where the Act speaks to the employer, the Commissioner or the
-- Minister, what is encoded is what that means for the employee.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 5 December 2025, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/EmA1968.txt; and the Employment (Retrenchment Reporting) Notification 2019
-- (S 200/2019), version in force from 1 November 2021, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/EmA1968-S200-2019.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The Act is large; this baseline keeps to what an employee most meets. Left out: s 9 and s 12; ss 16-19
-- (damages on breach, transfer of employment, contractors); s 20A and the salary-period rules; ss 25, 28, 30, 31 in
-- detail; s 33 (priority in insolvency); s 36 rosters, s 38(1) hours limits, ss 38(5), 38(8), 39-41A; s 46; Parts 5-8
-- (contractors, part-time employees, domestic workers, children and young persons); s 76(1)(c)(ii), s 76(3), ss 77-80
-- except s 80(3), s 82, ss 84-87A (including childcare leave); s 88 (public holidays); ss 95, 96 (records, pay
-- slips); Parts 13-16 (inspection, offences, administrative penalties, general) and Part 1 machinery. Every number
-- the Act lets the Minister prescribe "in substitution" is an input carrying the Act's own figure; the regulations
-- were not deposited. Confinements before 22 August 2015 and retrenchment notices before 1 November 2021 return an
-- explicit "not covered" value.
--
-- BASELINE. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the employee,
-- with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human
-- gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Employment Act 1968 -- the employee's questions`

§§ `2(1) -- am I an employee under this Act`

-- "employee" means a person who has entered into or works under a contract of service with an employer and
-- includes a workman, and any officer or employee of the Government ... declared by the President to be employees
-- ..., but does not include any of the following: (a) any seafarer; (b) any domestic worker; ... (d) any person
-- belonging to any other class of persons whom the Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, declare not to be
-- employees.
-- Gloss: "contract of service" is an employment contract (as against a contract for services, the self-employed);
-- a "domestic worker" works in or in connection with the domestic services of private premises.
DECLARE `My standing` HAS
    `I have entered into or work under a contract of service with an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a seafarer`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a domestic worker`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a Government officer or employee`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Conditional on an official act: the President's declaration, the Minister's Gazette notification.
    `the President has declared my category of Government officer to be employees` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has declared by Gazette notification a class I belong to not to be employees` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `me` IS A `My standing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an employee under the Employment Act` IF
        `me`'s `I have entered into or work under a contract of service with an employer`
    AND (    NOT `me`'s `I am a Government officer or employee`
         OR  `me`'s `the President has declared my category of Government officer to be employees`)
    AND NOT `me`'s `I am a seafarer`
    AND NOT `me`'s `I am a domestic worker`
    AND NOT `me`'s `the Minister has declared by Gazette notification a class I belong to not to be employees`

§§ `8, 10 -- the notice I am owed`

-- s 8: "Every term of a contract of service which provides a condition of service which is less favourable to an
-- employee than any of the conditions of service prescribed by this Act is illegal and void to the extent that it is
-- so less favourable."
-- s 10(2): the length of notice "is to be determined by any provision made for the notice in the terms of the
-- contract of service, or, in the absence of such provision, must be in accordance with subsection (3)".
-- s 10(3): at least (a) one day's notice if employed "for less than 26 weeks"; (b) one week's notice if "26 weeks or
-- more but less than 2 years"; (c) 2 weeks' notice if "2 years or more but less than 5 years"; (d) 4 weeks' notice
-- if "5 years or more".
-- Gloss: "notice" is the written warning either side must give to end the contract; the day it is given counts
-- (s 10(5)). The bands are worked out from completed weeks and completed years, which the employee states.
DECLARE `My service` HAS
    `completed weeks of employment` IS A NUMBER
    `completed years of employment` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `My contract's notice term` HAS
    `the contract provides for notice`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice the contract provides, in days`        IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the service` IS A `My service`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the minimum notice under section 10(3), in days` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the service`'s `completed years of employment` AT LEAST 5 THEN 28
        IF `the service`'s `completed years of employment` AT LEAST 2 THEN 14
        IF `the service`'s `completed weeks of employment` AT LEAST 26 THEN 7
        OTHERWISE 1

GIVEN `the term` IS A `My contract's notice term`, `the service` IS A `My service`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days of notice am I owed` IS
    IF      `the term`'s `the contract provides for notice`
        AND `the term`'s `the notice the contract provides, in days` AT LEAST `the minimum notice under section 10(3), in days` `the service`
    THEN `the term`'s `the notice the contract provides, in days`
    -- a shorter contractual term is void under s 8, which leaves no provision, so s 10(3) applies
    ELSE `the minimum notice under section 10(3), in days` `the service`

§§ `11 -- salary in lieu of notice`

-- s 11(1): either party may end the contract without notice "by paying to the other party a sum equal to the
-- amount of salary at the gross rate of pay which would have accrued to the employee during the period of the
-- notice"; for a monthly-rated employee with notice of less than a month, each day is "the gross rate of pay for
-- one day's work".
-- Gloss: "gross rate of pay" is pay before deductions (s 2(1)). Read here as days of notice times the daily gross
-- rate, which is the Act's own rule for a monthly-rated employee with less than a month's notice; for longer notice
-- the employee supplies the daily equivalent (inference, labelled).
GIVEN `my gross rate of pay for one day` IS A NUMBER
      `the term` IS A `My contract's notice term`
      `the service` IS A `My service`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I be paid in lieu of notice` IS
    `my gross rate of pay for one day` TIMES `How many days of notice am I owed` `the term` `the service`

§§ `13 -- being treated as having broken the contract`

-- s 13(1): "An employer is deemed to have broken the employer's contract of service with the employee if the
-- employer fails to pay salary in accordance with Part 3."
-- s 13(2): an employee is deemed to have broken the contract "if the employee is absent from work for more than
-- 2 days continuously without prior leave from the employer and -- (a) the employee has no reasonable excuse for
-- the absence; or (b) the employee does not inform and does not attempt to inform the employer of the excuse".
-- Gloss: "deemed to have broken" means treated by the Act as if I walked out. Whether an excuse is reasonable is a
-- judgment for whoever decides the dispute, so it is a conditional input, never guessed.
DECLARE `My absence` HAS
    `days I was absent continuously`                                  IS A NUMBER
    `I had prior leave from my employer`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `if it is accepted that I had a reasonable excuse for the absence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I informed or attempted to inform my employer of the excuse`     IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the absence` IS A `My absence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as having broken my contract by being absent` IF
        `the absence`'s `days I was absent continuously` GREATER THAN 2
    AND NOT `the absence`'s `I had prior leave from my employer`
    AND (    NOT `the absence`'s `if it is accepted that I had a reasonable excuse for the absence`
         OR  NOT `the absence`'s `I informed or attempted to inform my employer of the excuse`)

§§ `15 -- leaving without notice because of danger`

-- s 15: "An employee may terminate his or her contract of service ... without notice where the employee or the
-- employee's dependant is immediately threatened by danger to the person by violence or disease that the employee
-- did not by his or her contract of service undertake to run."
DECLARE `The danger` HAS
    `the threat is to me or my dependant`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the threat is immediate`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is danger to the person by violence or disease`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `I undertook by my contract of service to run that risk`       IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the danger` IS A `The danger`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I leave without notice because of danger` IF
        `the danger`'s `the threat is to me or my dependant`
    AND `the danger`'s `the threat is immediate`
    AND `the danger`'s `it is danger to the person by violence or disease`
    AND NOT `the danger`'s `I undertook by my contract of service to run that risk`

§§ `14 -- dismissal, suspension and the wrongful dismissal claim`

-- s 14(1): "An employer may after due inquiry dismiss without notice an employee ... on the grounds of misconduct
-- inconsistent with the fulfilment of the express or implied conditions of the employee's service, except that
-- instead of dismissing an employee an employer may -- (a) instantly down-grade the employee; or (b) instantly
-- suspend the employee from work without payment of salary for a period not exceeding one week."
-- s 14(8): for the inquiry the employer "(a) may suspend the employee from work for -- (i) a period not exceeding one
-- week; or (ii) such longer period as the Commissioner may determine on an application by the employer; but (b) must
-- pay the employee at least half the employee's salary during the period". s 14(9): if the inquiry "does not
-- disclose any misconduct", the employer "must immediately restore ... the full amount of the salary so withheld".
-- Gloss: "due inquiry" is a proper inquiry by the employer into the allegation before acting on it. Whether the
-- conduct is misconduct of that kind is the inquiry's finding, so it is a conditional input.
DECLARE `My discipline` HAS
    `a due inquiry was held`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `if the inquiry found misconduct inconsistent with the conditions of my service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days I was suspended without salary as the penalty`                           IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the discipline` IS A `My discipline`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my employer dismiss me without notice for misconduct` IF
        `the discipline`'s `a due inquiry was held`
    AND `the discipline`'s `if the inquiry found misconduct inconsistent with the conditions of my service`

GIVEN `the discipline` IS A `My discipline`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my suspension without pay as a penalty lawful` IF
        `Can my employer dismiss me without notice for misconduct` `the discipline`
    AND `the discipline`'s `days I was suspended without salary as the penalty` AT MOST 7

DECLARE `My suspension pending inquiry` HAS
    `my salary for the period of the suspension`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `days suspended`                                                                IS A NUMBER
    `if the Commissioner determined a longer period on my employer's application`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the inquiry disclosed misconduct on my part`                                   IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the suspension` IS A `My suspension pending inquiry`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my suspension pending inquiry within the time allowed` IF
        `the suspension`'s `days suspended` AT MOST 7
    OR  `the suspension`'s `if the Commissioner determined a longer period on my employer's application`

GIVEN `the suspension` IS A `My suspension pending inquiry`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the least I must be paid for my suspension pending inquiry` IS
    IF   `the suspension`'s `the inquiry disclosed misconduct on my part`
    THEN `the suspension`'s `my salary for the period of the suspension` DIVIDED BY 2
    -- s 14(9): no misconduct disclosed, so the half withheld must be restored
    ELSE `the suspension`'s `my salary for the period of the suspension`

-- s 14(2): "subject to section 3 of the Employment Claims Act 2016, where a relevant employee considers that he or
-- she has been dismissed without just cause or excuse ... the employee may lodge a claim" for reinstatement or
-- compensation.
-- s 14(2A): a relevant employee means "(a) an employee employed in a managerial or an executive position -- (i) who
-- is dismissed with notice; or (ii) who is dismissed without notice but receives payment of any salary in lieu of
-- notice, after having served that employer for at least 6 months in any position ...; (b) an employee employed in
-- a managerial or an executive position who is dismissed without notice and without salary in lieu of such notice;
-- or (c) an employee not employed in a managerial or an executive position."
-- Gloss: "managerial or executive position" is not defined in the deposit, so it is asked as a fact. The answer is
-- "yes, subject to s 3 of the Employment Claims Act 2016", which was not deposited.
DECLARE `My dismissal` HAS
    `I was in a managerial or an executive position`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was dismissed with notice`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was dismissed without notice but received salary in lieu`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `I had served that employer for at least 6 months in any position` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the dismissal` IS A `My dismissal`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I claim for wrongful dismissal` IF
        NOT `the dismissal`'s `I was in a managerial or an executive position`
    OR  (    NOT `the dismissal`'s `I was dismissed with notice`
         AND NOT `the dismissal`'s `I was dismissed without notice but received salary in lieu`)
    OR  `the dismissal`'s `I had served that employer for at least 6 months in any position`

§§ `45 -- retrenchment benefit`

-- s 45: "No employee who has been in continuous service with an employer for less than 2 years is entitled to any
-- retrenchment benefit on his or her dismissal on the ground of redundancy or by reason of any reorganisation".
-- Gloss: a "retrenchment benefit" is a payment on being let go for redundancy. The Act only bars it below 2 years;
-- it nowhere says when one is owed or how much, so beyond the bar the answer is that the Act does not say.
DECLARE `Retrenchment benefit answer` IS ONE OF
    `none -- under 2 years of continuous service (s 45)`
    `not decided by this Act -- it depends on my contract or a collective agreement`
    `not a retrenchment -- s 45 does not speak to it`

GIVEN `years of continuous service` IS A NUMBER
      `I was dismissed for redundancy or a reorganisation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Retrenchment benefit answer`
DECIDE `Am I entitled to a retrenchment benefit` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `I was dismissed for redundancy or a reorganisation` THEN `not a retrenchment -- s 45 does not speak to it`
        IF `years of continuous service` LESS THAN 2 THEN `none -- under 2 years of continuous service (s 45)`
        OTHERWISE `not decided by this Act -- it depends on my contract or a collective agreement`

§§ `21-24 -- when I must be paid`

-- s 21(1): salary other than overtime "must be paid before the expiry of the 7th day after the last day of the
-- salary period"; (2) overtime "not later than 14 days after the last day of the salary period"; (3) on completion
-- of the contract, "on completion of the contract".
-- s 22: on dismissal, "on the day of dismissal or, if this is not possible, within 3 days thereafter, not being a
-- rest day or public holiday or other holiday".
-- s 23(1): where I resign under s 11 or after due notice, "on the day on which the contract of service is
-- terminated"; (2) where I leave without due notice, "before the expiry of the 7th day after".
-- s 24: "Despite sections 22 and 23", where the Comptroller of Income Tax's permission under s 68(7) of the Income
-- Tax Act 1947 is needed, payment "must not be delayed more than 30 days after the notice has been given to and
-- received by the Comptroller".
-- Days are counted from the day named for each occasion; for s 22 only days that are not rest days or holidays
-- count. Whether s 68(7) applies is a borrowed term, asked as a fact (the occasion chosen).
DECLARE `Payment occasion` IS ONE OF
    `my salary for a salary period`
    `my overtime pay for a salary period`
    `my salary on completion of my contract`
    `my salary after I was dismissed`
    `my salary after I resigned with due notice or salary in lieu`
    `my salary after I left without due notice`
    `my final salary where income tax clearance is needed`

GIVEN `the occasion` IS A `Payment occasion`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the days allowed to pay me` IS
    CONSIDER `the occasion`
    WHEN `my salary for a salary period` THEN 7
    WHEN `my overtime pay for a salary period` THEN 14
    WHEN `my salary on completion of my contract` THEN 0
    WHEN `my salary after I was dismissed` THEN 3
    WHEN `my salary after I resigned with due notice or salary in lieu` THEN 0
    WHEN `my salary after I left without due notice` THEN 7
    WHEN `my final salary where income tax clearance is needed` THEN 30

GIVEN `the occasion` IS A `Payment occasion`, `the days taken to pay me` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I paid late` IF
    `the days taken to pay me` GREATER THAN `the days allowed to pay me` `the occasion`

-- s 13(1), from my side: paying late under Part 3 is the employer's deemed breach.
GIVEN `the occasion` IS A `Payment occasion`, `the days taken to pay me` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employer treated as having broken my contract` IF
    `Was I paid late` `the occasion` `the days taken to pay me`

-- s 21(1) as a duty with a deadline, counted in days from the last day of the salary period.
DECLARE `Party to my contract` IS ONE OF `my employer`, `me`
DECLARE `Act under section 21` IS ONE OF `pay my salary for the salary period`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to my contract` `Act under section 21`
DECIDE `my employer's duty to pay my salary` IS
    PARTY  `my employer`
    MUST   `pay my salary for the salary period`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `my employer`

§§ `26, 27, 29, 32 -- what may be taken from my pay`

-- s 26(1): "No deduction is to be made by an employer from the salary of an employee, unless the deduction is
-- authorised by or under any provision of this Act or is required" by a court order or a tax-recovery declaration.
-- s 27(1) lists the authorised deductions: (a) absence; (b) damage to or loss of goods entrusted, or loss of money
-- to be accounted for, "directly attributable to the employee's neglect or default"; (d) "with the employee's
-- written consent" for house accommodation; (e) with written consent for amenities and services the Commissioner
-- may authorise; (f) recovery of an advance, loan or unearned employment benefit, or an overpayment; (h) CPF
-- contributions; (i) any other deduction "made with the employee's written consent"; (j) with written consent, dues
-- to a registered cooperative society; (k) prescribed deductions.
-- s 27(1A): written consent for (d), (e), (i) or (j) "may be withdrawn by the employee giving written notice of the
-- withdrawal to the employer at any time before the deduction is made"; (1B) I cannot be penalised for withdrawing.
DECLARE `Kind of deduction` IS ONE OF
    `for absence from work`
    `for damage to or loss of goods entrusted to me, or money I must account for, through my neglect or default`
    `for house accommodation supplied by my employer`
    `for amenities and services supplied by my employer that the Commissioner has authorised`
    `to recover an advance, loan or unearned employment benefit, or an overpayment of salary`
    `for CPF contributions payable on my behalf`
    `for dues to a registered cooperative society`
    `a prescribed deduction`
    `required by a court order or a tax-recovery declaration`
    `any other deduction`

DECLARE `My consent` HAS
    `I gave written consent`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `I gave written notice withdrawing it before the deduction was made` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the consent` IS A `My consent`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my written consent stands` IF
        `the consent`'s `I gave written consent`
    AND NOT `the consent`'s `I gave written notice withdrawing it before the deduction was made`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of deduction`, `the consent` IS A `My consent`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my employer make this deduction from my salary` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `for house accommodation supplied by my employer` THEN `my written consent stands` `the consent`
    WHEN `for amenities and services supplied by my employer that the Commissioner has authorised` THEN `my written consent stands` `the consent`
    WHEN `for dues to a registered cooperative society` THEN `my written consent stands` `the consent`
    WHEN `any other deduction` THEN `my written consent stands` `the consent`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The fractions the Act lets the Minister substitute: s 29(1) "one-quarter (or such other proportion prescribed in
-- substitution by the Minister) of one month's wages"; s 32(1) "50% (or such other percentage prescribed in
-- substitution by the Minister)". No substitution was deposited, so these are inputs carrying the Act's figures.
DECLARE `Prescribed proportions` HAS
    `the damages ceiling as a fraction of one month's wages` IS A NUMBER
    `the overall ceiling as a fraction of the salary for the period` IS A NUMBER

`the proportions as the Act states them` MEANS
    `Prescribed proportions` WITH
        `the damages ceiling as a fraction of one month's wages`         IS 0.25
        `the overall ceiling as a fraction of the salary for the period` IS 0.5

-- s 29(1): a deduction under s 27(1)(b) "must not exceed the amount of the damages or loss caused to the employer
-- by the neglect or default of the employee and, except with the Commissioner's permission, must not in any case
-- exceed one-quarter ... of one month's wages and must not be made until the employee has been given an
-- opportunity of showing cause against the deduction."
-- Gloss: "showing cause" is explaining why the deduction should not be made.
DECLARE `The damages deduction` HAS
    `the loss my neglect or default caused my employer`              IS A NUMBER
    `the amount my employer proposes to deduct`                      IS A NUMBER
    `my wages for one month`                                         IS A NUMBER
    `if the Commissioner has permitted a larger deduction`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was given an opportunity of showing cause against it`         IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the deduction` IS A `The damages deduction`, `the proportions` IS A `Prescribed proportions`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my employer deduct this amount for damage or loss I caused` IF
        `the deduction`'s `the amount my employer proposes to deduct` AT MOST `the deduction`'s `the loss my neglect or default caused my employer`
    AND (    `the deduction`'s `if the Commissioner has permitted a larger deduction`
         OR  `the deduction`'s `the amount my employer proposes to deduct`
                 AT MOST `the deduction`'s `my wages for one month` TIMES `the proportions`'s `the damages ceiling as a fraction of one month's wages`)
    AND `the deduction`'s `I was given an opportunity of showing cause against it`

-- s 32(1): the total of all deductions in one salary period, "other than deductions under section 27(1)(a), (f) or
-- (j), must not exceed 50% ... of the salary payable"; (2) not for "the last salary due ... on termination ... or on
-- completion".
GIVEN `the deductions counted by section 32` IS A NUMBER
      `the salary payable for the period` IS A NUMBER
      `this is my last salary on termination or completion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proportions` IS A `Prescribed proportions`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the deductions from my salary this period within the overall limit` IF
        `this is my last salary on termination or completion`
    OR  `the deductions counted by section 32`
            AT MOST `the salary payable for the period` TIMES `the proportions`'s `the overall ceiling as a fraction of the salary for the period`

§§ `35 -- do the rest day, hours and overtime rules cover me`

-- s 2(1) "workman": (a) a person "engaged in manual labour, including any artisan or apprentice"; (b) a person,
-- "other than clerical staff, employed in the operation or maintenance of mechanically-propelled vehicles used for
-- the transport of passengers for hire or for commercial purposes"; (c) a person "employed partly for manual labour
-- and partly for the purpose of supervising in person any workman"; proviso: a person employed "partly as a workman
-- and partly in some other capacity" is deemed a workman unless the workman time "has on no occasion amounted to or
-- exceeded one-half" of the time worked in any salary period.
-- s 35: Part 4 applies "(a) to workmen who are in receipt of a salary not exceeding $4,500 a month (excluding
-- overtime payments, bonus payments, annual wage supplements, productivity incentive payments and any allowance
-- however described) or such other amount as the Minister may prescribe; and (b) to every employee (other than a
-- workman or a person employed in a managerial or an executive position) who receives a salary not exceeding
-- $2,600 a month" (same exclusions) "or such other amount as the Minister may prescribe".
DECLARE `My kind of work` IS ONE OF
    `manual labour, as an artisan, apprentice or otherwise`
    `operating or maintaining vehicles for passenger hire or commercial transport, not clerical`
    `partly manual labour and partly supervising workmen in person`
    `partly as a workman and partly in another capacity`
    `none of these`

DECLARE `My work` HAS
    `the kind of work`                                                         IS A `My kind of work`
    `in some salary period my workman's time reached half or more of my time`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `my monthly salary without overtime, bonus, AWS, productivity incentive or allowances` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the work` IS A `My work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a workman` IF
    CONSIDER `the work`'s `the kind of work`
    WHEN `partly as a workman and partly in another capacity` THEN `the work`'s `in some salary period my workman's time reached half or more of my time`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE `Prescribed salary caps` HAS
    `the cap for workmen`        IS A NUMBER
    `the cap for other employees` IS A NUMBER

`the caps as the Act states them` MEANS
    `Prescribed salary caps` WITH
        `the cap for workmen`         IS 4500
        `the cap for other employees` IS 2600

GIVEN `the work` IS A `My work`, `the caps` IS A `Prescribed salary caps`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the rest day, hours and overtime rules cover me` IF
    IF   `Am I a workman` `the work`
    THEN `the work`'s `my monthly salary without overtime, bonus, AWS, productivity incentive or allowances` AT MOST `the caps`'s `the cap for workmen`
    ELSE     NOT `the work`'s `I am employed in a managerial or an executive position`
         AND `the work`'s `my monthly salary without overtime, bonus, AWS, productivity incentive or allowances` AT MOST `the caps`'s `the cap for other employees`

§§ `38(4), 38(6), Fourth Schedule -- overtime pay`

-- s 38(4): work beyond the daily or weekly limits at the employer's request "must be paid for ... at the rate of not
-- less than one and a half times the employee's hourly basic rate of pay irrespective of the basis on which the
-- employee's rate of pay is fixed".
-- Fourth Schedule (s 38(6)), the same for a workman and a non-workman: monthly rate -- "12 x monthly basic rate of
-- pay" over "52 x 44"; piece rates -- "The total weekly pay at the basic rate of pay received divided by the total
-- number of hours worked in the week"; hourly -- "Actual hourly basic rate of pay"; daily -- "Daily basic rate of pay
-- divided by the number of working hours per day".
-- Gloss: "basic rate of pay" is pay without allowances, overtime or bonuses (s 2(1)).
DECLARE `How my pay is fixed` IS ONE OF
    `monthly`     HAS `my monthly basic rate of pay` IS A NUMBER
    `piece rates` HAS `my weekly pay at the basic rate` IS A NUMBER, `hours I worked in the week` IS A NUMBER
    `hourly`      HAS `my hourly basic rate` IS A NUMBER
    `daily`       HAS `my daily basic rate of pay` IS A NUMBER, `my working hours per day` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the basis` IS A `How my pay is fixed`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my hourly basic rate of pay` IS
    CONSIDER `the basis`
    WHEN `monthly` m       THEN (12 TIMES m) DIVIDED BY (52 TIMES 44)
    WHEN `piece rates` w h THEN w DIVIDED BY h
    WHEN `hourly` r        THEN r
    WHEN `daily` d h       THEN d DIVIDED BY h

GIVEN `the extra hours` IS A NUMBER, `the basis` IS A `How my pay is fixed`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the least I must be paid for my overtime` IS
    1.5 TIMES `What is my hourly basic rate of pay` `the basis` TIMES `the extra hours`

§§ `37 -- working on my rest day`

-- s 37(2): at my own request, (a) up to half my normal hours: "the basic rate of pay for half a day's work"; (b) more
-- than half, up to normal hours: "one day's work"; (c) beyond normal hours: one day's work plus "not less than one
-- and a half times the employee's hourly basic rate of pay for each hour or part thereof" beyond normal hours.
-- s 37(3): at my employer's request, the same steps at one day, 2 days, and 2 days plus the overtime rate.
-- s 37(3A): "normal hours of work" are the hours agreed as the usual hours per day, "or in the absence of any such
-- agreement, is deemed to be 8 hours a day". s 37(4): (3) does not apply to Government or statutory-body essential
-- services employees, who get a day off instead -- not encoded.
-- Gloss: a "rest day" is my one whole unpaid day off each week (s 36).
DECLARE `Whose request` IS ONE OF `my own request`, `my employer's request`

DECLARE `My rest day work` HAS
    `at whose request`                       IS A `Whose request`
    `the hours I worked on the rest day`     IS A NUMBER
    `the usual hours per day agreed, if any` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `my basic rate of pay for one day's work` IS A NUMBER
    `my hourly basic rate of pay`            IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the work` IS A `My rest day work`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `my normal hours of work` IS
    CONSIDER `the work`'s `the usual hours per day agreed, if any`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 8
    WHEN JUST h  THEN h

GIVEN `the hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `each hour or part thereof` IS
    IF   TRUNC `the hours` 0 LESS THAN `the hours`
    THEN TRUNC `the hours` 0 PLUS 1
    ELSE TRUNC `the hours` 0

GIVEN `the work` IS A `My rest day work`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What must I be paid for working on my rest day` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the work`'s `the hours I worked on the rest day` AT MOST (`my normal hours of work` `the work` DIVIDED BY 2)
            THEN `days of basic pay` TIMES 0.5 TIMES `the work`'s `my basic rate of pay for one day's work`
        IF `the work`'s `the hours I worked on the rest day` AT MOST `my normal hours of work` `the work`
            THEN `days of basic pay` TIMES `the work`'s `my basic rate of pay for one day's work`
        OTHERWISE
                 `days of basic pay` TIMES `the work`'s `my basic rate of pay for one day's work`
            PLUS 1.5 TIMES `the work`'s `my hourly basic rate of pay`
                     TIMES `each hour or part thereof` (`the work`'s `the hours I worked on the rest day` MINUS `my normal hours of work` `the work`)
    WHERE
        `days of basic pay` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the work`'s `at whose request`
            WHEN `my own request`        THEN 1
            WHEN `my employer's request` THEN 2

§§ `88A -- annual leave`

-- s 88A(1): an employee who has served "not less than 3 months" is entitled to "(a) 7 days of paid annual leave, for
-- the first 12 months of continuous service with the same employer; (b) ... an additional one day of paid annual
-- leave, for every subsequent 12 months ...; (c) a maximum of 14 days".
-- (2): having served 3 months "but has not completed 12 months of continuous service in any year", annual leave "in
-- proportion to the number of completed months of service in that year"; (3) a fraction under one-half is
-- disregarded, one-half or more is one day. (4) unpaid leave at my request does not count as service.
-- (5): "An employee forfeits the employee's entitlement to annual leave if the employee absents himself or herself
-- from work without the employer's permission, or without reasonable excuse, for more than 20% of the working days".
-- (8): if "dismissed on any ground other than misconduct" before taking it all, the employer "must pay ... gross rate
-- of pay in respect of every day of that leave not taken".
-- Reading (inference, labelled): the proportion in (2) is taken of the full entitlement for that year of service.
DECLARE `My leave year` HAS
    `completed months of service with this employer`        IS A NUMBER
    `which year of continuous service this is`               IS A NUMBER
    `completed months of service in that year`               IS A NUMBER
    `I was absent without permission or reasonable excuse for more than 20% of the working days` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the year` IS A `My leave year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the full annual leave for that year of service` IS
    min (7 PLUS (`the year`'s `which year of continuous service this is` MINUS 1)) 14

-- Integer rounding half up, kept in whole numbers: MODULO is unreliable on fractions with this toolchain.
GIVEN `the numerator` IS A NUMBER, `the denominator` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `rounded half up` IS
    IF   2 TIMES (`the numerator` MODULO `the denominator`) AT LEAST `the denominator`
    THEN `whole part` PLUS 1
    ELSE `whole part`
    WHERE
        `whole part` MEANS (`the numerator` MINUS (`the numerator` MODULO `the denominator`)) DIVIDED BY `the denominator`

GIVEN `the year` IS A `My leave year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days of annual leave do I get` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the year`'s `completed months of service with this employer` LESS THAN 3 THEN 0
        IF `the year`'s `I was absent without permission or reasonable excuse for more than 20% of the working days` THEN 0
        IF `the year`'s `completed months of service in that year` AT LEAST 12 THEN `the full annual leave for that year of service` `the year`
        OTHERWISE `rounded half up`
                      (`the full annual leave for that year of service` `the year` TIMES `the year`'s `completed months of service in that year`)
                      12

GIVEN `days of annual leave not taken` IS A NUMBER
      `my gross rate of pay for one day` IS A NUMBER
      `I was dismissed for misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What must I be paid for annual leave not taken when I am dismissed` IS
    IF   `I was dismissed for misconduct`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `days of annual leave not taken` TIMES `my gross rate of pay for one day`

§§ `89 -- sick leave`

-- s 89(1): after "not less than 6 months", after examination by a medical practitioner, paid sick leave as certified,
-- "not exceeding in the aggregate -- (a) if no hospitalisation is necessary, 14 days in each year; or (b) if
-- hospitalisation is necessary, the lesser of ... (i) 60 days in each year; (ii) the aggregate of 14 days plus the
-- number of days on which the employee is hospitalised".
-- s 89(2): 3 to under 4 months: 5 days, or the lesser of 15 and 5 plus days hospitalised; 4 to under 5 months: 8,
-- or the lesser of 30 and 8 plus; 5 to under 6 months: 11, or the lesser of 45 and 11 plus.
-- Gloss: "hospitalised" includes being warded in prescribed circumstances or quarantined (s 89(3)).
DECLARE `Sick leave row` HAS
    `days without hospitalisation`   IS A NUMBER
    `ceiling with hospitalisation`   IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `months served` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Sick leave row`
DECIDE `the sick leave row for` IS
    --                                             without, ceiling
    BRANCH IF `months served` AT LEAST 6 THEN `Sick leave row` OF 14, 60
           IF `months served` AT LEAST 5 THEN `Sick leave row` OF 11, 45
           IF `months served` AT LEAST 4 THEN `Sick leave row` OF 8,  30
           IF `months served` AT LEAST 3 THEN `Sick leave row` OF 5,  15
           OTHERWISE                          `Sick leave row` OF 0,  0

DECLARE `My sickness` HAS
    `completed months of service with this employer`  IS A NUMBER
    `I was examined by a medical practitioner`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `hospitalisation is necessary`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `days I am hospitalised`                           IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the sickness` IS A `My sickness`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days of paid sick leave can I take in the year` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the sickness`'s `I was examined by a medical practitioner` THEN 0
        IF `the sickness`'s `hospitalisation is necessary`
            THEN min (`the row`'s `ceiling with hospitalisation`)
                     (`the row`'s `days without hospitalisation` PLUS `the sickness`'s `days I am hospitalised`)
        OTHERWISE `the row`'s `days without hospitalisation`
    WHERE
        `the row` MEANS `the sick leave row for` (`the sickness`'s `completed months of service with this employer`)

§§ `76, 80(3), 81, 83 -- maternity`

-- s 76(1A): every female employee is entitled to payment "at her gross rate of pay" for the benefit period: in each
-- of the arrangements in s 76(1)(a), (b) and (c), 8 weeks.
-- s 76(2B): for a child delivered on or after 22 August 2015 (or with an estimated delivery date on or after it), no
-- pay "if she has not served her employer for a period of at least 3 months preceding the day of her confinement".
-- s 76(4): "Subject to any collective agreement or award to the contrary", no payment if at the confinement "(a) she
-- has 2 or more living children; and (b) those children were born during more than one previous confinement"; (5)
-- not for classes the Minister specifies by Gazette notification.
-- s 77(1): payable "for every day of the benefit period, including holidays".
-- s 80(3): an employee who omits the notices in s 80(1) (one week before absence) or (2) (date of confinement, as
-- soon as practicable) "is entitled to only half the amount ... unless she was prevented by any sufficient cause".
-- s 83: working for any other employer after starting the absence, "she forfeits her claim to any payment".
-- Gloss: "confinement" is giving birth. The earlier qualifying rules (s 76(2), (2A)) are not encoded, so an earlier
-- confinement returns the explicit "not covered" value. s 76(3) (extra pay for a day worked in the benefit period
-- before confinement) and no-pay leave days under s 77(1) are not encoded.
DECLARE `My confinement` HAS
    `I delivered on or after 22 August 2015, or my estimated delivery date was on or after that day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I served my employer for at least 3 months before the day of my confinement`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `I had 2 or more living children, born in more than one previous confinement`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a collective agreement, award or Gazette notification takes me out of section 76(4)`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `I gave the notices section 80 requires`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `if it is accepted that sufficient cause prevented me from giving them`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `I worked for another employer after I began my maternity absence`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `my gross rate of pay for one day`                                                               IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Maternity pay answer` IS ONE OF
    `paid`    HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `nothing is payable`
    `not covered by this encoding -- confinement before 22 August 2015`

GIVEN `the confinement` IS A `My confinement`
GIVETH A `Maternity pay answer`
DECIDE `How much maternity pay must my employer give me` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the confinement`'s `I delivered on or after 22 August 2015, or my estimated delivery date was on or after that day`
            THEN `not covered by this encoding -- confinement before 22 August 2015`
        IF NOT `the confinement`'s `I served my employer for at least 3 months before the day of my confinement`
            THEN `nothing is payable`
        IF      `the confinement`'s `I had 2 or more living children, born in more than one previous confinement`
            AND NOT `the confinement`'s `a collective agreement, award or Gazette notification takes me out of section 76(4)`
            THEN `nothing is payable`
        IF `the confinement`'s `I worked for another employer after I began my maternity absence`
            THEN `nothing is payable`
        IF      NOT `the confinement`'s `I gave the notices section 80 requires`
            AND NOT `the confinement`'s `if it is accepted that sufficient cause prevented me from giving them`
            THEN `paid` (`the full benefit` DIVIDED BY 2)
        OTHERWISE `paid` `the full benefit`
    WHERE
        `the full benefit` MEANS 56 TIMES `the confinement`'s `my gross rate of pay for one day`

-- s 81: "when a female employee absents herself from work in accordance with the provisions of this Part it is not
-- lawful for her employer to give her notice of dismissal during her absence or on such a day that the notice will
-- expire during her absence."
GIVEN `I am absent in accordance with Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice of dismissal was given during my absence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice would expire during my absence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the notice of dismissal I was given unlawful because of my maternity absence` IF
        `I am absent in accordance with Part 9`
    AND (`the notice of dismissal was given during my absence` OR `the notice would expire during my absence`)

§§ `95A -- my key employment terms`

-- s 95A(1): applies to every employee "(a) who enters into a contract of service with the employer on or after
-- 1 April 2016; and (b) who is employed under that contract for a period not shorter than the prescribed minimum
-- period of service". (2): a written record of the key employment terms "not later than 14 days after the day that
-- the employee starts employment ..., or within such other period as may be prescribed in substitution". (5): the
-- employer "is taken to have failed to comply ... if the written record given is incomplete or inaccurate, whether or
-- not the employer knew".
-- Gloss: "key employment terms" are the terms the regulations prescribe (s 95A(7)); an electronic record or a
-- website the employer authorises and tells me of will do (s 95A(3)). The minimum period and any substituted period
-- are prescribed; the regulations were not deposited, so both are inputs.
DECLARE `My key terms` HAS
    `my contract of service was entered into on or after 1 April 2016`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am employed for at least the prescribed minimum period of service`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the period prescribed in substitution for 14 days, if any`               IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `a written record was given to me`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after I started employment when it was given`                        IS A NUMBER
    `the record was complete and accurate`                                     IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Key terms answer` IS ONE OF
    `section 95A does not apply to me`
    `my employer complied`
    `my employer failed to comply`

GIVEN `the terms` IS A `My key terms`
GIVETH A `Key terms answer`
DECIDE `Did my employer give me my key employment terms as section 95A requires` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (    `the terms`'s `my contract of service was entered into on or after 1 April 2016`
                AND `the terms`'s `I am employed for at least the prescribed minimum period of service`)
            THEN `section 95A does not apply to me`
        IF      `the terms`'s `a written record was given to me`
            AND `the terms`'s `days after I started employment when it was given` AT MOST `the period allowed`
            AND `the terms`'s `the record was complete and accurate`
            THEN `my employer complied`
        OTHERWISE `my employer failed to comply`
    WHERE
        `the period allowed` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the terms`'s `the period prescribed in substitution for 14 days, if any`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 14
            WHEN JUST d  THEN d

§§ `96A and the Retrenchment Reporting Notification 2019 -- reporting my retrenchment`

-- s 96A(1): the Commissioner "may, by notification in the Gazette, require any employer ... to furnish ... such
-- information on the retrenchment of any employee ... as may be specified"; (2) every employer to whom it applies
-- "must comply".
-- Notification para 2(1): "retrench" means to terminate the contract "at the initiative of the employer because of
-- redundancy or any reorganisation"; "working day" means "a day other than a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday".
-- Para 2(2): "employee" is one under a contract "(a) that does not specify an end date for the contract; or (b) that
-- has a term of employment of at least 6 months". Para 2(3): whether the employer has 10 or more employees "is to be
-- worked out as at the time when a notice of retrenchment is given". Para 3(1): every employer must report "if, on or
-- after 1 November 2021, the employer gives any of its employees a notice of his or her retrenchment, regardless when
-- the notice takes effect". Para 4: "not later than 5 working days after the day that the employer gives the notice".
-- Days are numbered from Monday 1 November 2021 = day 0, so day modulo 7 is 5 or 6 on a weekend. A notice before
-- day 0 falls under the earlier text of the Notification, which was not deposited: "not covered".
-- Reading (inference, labelled): para 2(2) narrows who counts towards the 10 as well as who is reported.
DECLARE `My retrenchment notice` HAS
    `I am an employee under section 2(1) of the Act`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `my contract specifies an end date`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `my term of employment in months`                                        IS A NUMBER
    `my employer's employees within the Notification on the day of notice`   IS A NUMBER
    `my employer ended my contract on its own initiative`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the reason is redundancy or a reorganisation`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the notice was given, counted from 1 November 2021`             IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Report answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes, my employer must report it`
    `no report is required`
    `not covered by this encoding -- notice given before 1 November 2021`

GIVEN `the notice` IS A `My retrenchment notice`
GIVETH A `Report answer`
DECIDE `Must my employer report my retrenchment to the Commissioner` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the notice`'s `the day the notice was given, counted from 1 November 2021` LESS THAN 0
            THEN `not covered by this encoding -- notice given before 1 November 2021`
        IF      `the notice`'s `I am an employee under section 2(1) of the Act`
            AND (    NOT `the notice`'s `my contract specifies an end date`
                 OR  `the notice`'s `my term of employment in months` AT LEAST 6)
            AND `the notice`'s `my employer's employees within the Notification on the day of notice` AT LEAST 10
            AND `the notice`'s `my employer ended my contract on its own initiative`
            AND `the notice`'s `the reason is redundancy or a reorganisation`
            THEN `yes, my employer must report it`
        OTHERWISE `no report is required`

GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER
      `public holidays` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a working day` IF
        `the day` MODULO 7 LESS THAN 5
    AND NOT elem `the day` `public holidays`

GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER
      `working days still to count` IS A NUMBER
      `public holidays` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the day that ends the count` IS
    IF   `working days still to count` AT MOST 0
    THEN `the day`
    ELSE IF   `is a working day` (`the day` PLUS 1) `public holidays`
         THEN `the day that ends the count` (`the day` PLUS 1) (`working days still to count` MINUS 1) `public holidays`
         ELSE `the day that ends the count` (`the day` PLUS 1) `working days still to count` `public holidays`

-- Public holidays are not in the deposit; they are supplied as day numbers.
GIVEN `the day the notice was given, counted from 1 November 2021` IS A NUMBER
      `public holidays` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By which day must my employer report my retrenchment` IS
    `the day that ends the count` `the day the notice was given, counted from 1 November 2021` 5 `public holidays`
